Delivered behavior:
- SqlReviewRecordRepository.SaveAsync accepts only a TrustedFirmId, the
  already-projected Tenancy PersistedReviewRecord, and a cancellation token.
- Persistence names, accepts, returns, and serializes no executable CaseReview
  type; ReviewPackageProjection.Project runs before the persistence boundary.
- SaveAsync independently refuses a projected record whose FirmId differs from
  the trusted scope, without echoing either identifier.
- Version assignment is firm-scoped and transactional: the repository writes
  max(PackageVersion) + 1 for the complete subject key and never updates an
  earlier version.
- A unique-version race fails closed and never overwrites the prior record.
- FindAsync scopes by FirmId plus RecordId; cross-firm and absent records both
  return the same null result.
- Ordered slips, box amounts, line entries, source box codes, and unmapped codes
  round-trip without sorting, merging, aggregation, or monetary alteration.
- No update, upsert, or delete path was added.

